047789,31.4230647249312,31.908013479957,32.3963124748942,32.8878826925466,33.3826439647044,33.8805151370437,34.381414227854,34.8852585807422,35.391965011452,35.9014499489318,36.4136295707766,36.9284199331628,37.4457370953864,37.9654972391109,38.4876167824223,39.0120124887835,;16,-1,121,2.664,2.724606,2.78337812502658,2.84032330449679,2.89545160238064,2.94877595280774,3.00031190119191,3.05007735242591,3.09809232747029,3.14437872944116,3.18896012009296,3.23186150739595,3.27310914472634,3.31273034201915,3.35075328908248,3.38720689113529,3.4221206165103,3.45552435635779,3.48744829609566,3.51792279827357,3.54697829645558,3.57464519967387,3.60095380696545,3.62593423147374,3.64961633357568,3.67202966248202,3.69320340575295,3.71316634617168,3.73194682542456,3.74957271404722,3.76607138711032,3.78146970513639,3.79579399975915,3.80907006365902,3.82132314433159,3.83257794127083,3.84285860617339,3.8521887457959,3.86059142712244,3.86808918452415,3.87470402861759,3.88045745655203,3.88537046347911,3.88946355498003,3.89275676024671,3.89526964583337,3.89702132981355,3.8980304961959,3.89831540946816,3.89789392915461,3.89678352428671,3.89500128769967,3.89256395008036,3.88948789370291,3.88578916579899,3.88148349151872,3.87658628644708,3.871112668648,3.86507747021538,3.85849524831645,3.8513802957181,3.84374665079196,3.83560810699792,3.82697822184977,3.81787032536944,3.80829752803943,3.79827272826499,3.78780861935976,3.77691769607004,3.76561226065395,3.75390442853323,3.74180613353543,3.72932913274539,3.71648501098487,3.70328518493931,3.68974090695092,3.67586326849692,3.66166320337154,3.64715149059021,3.6323387570336,3.61723547984901,3.60185198862592,3.58619846736179,3.57028495623383,3.5541213531916,3.53771741538479,3.52108276043969,3.50422686759741,3.48715907872608,3.46988859921866,3.45242449878725,3.43477571216446,3.41695103972134,3.39895914801117,3.38080857024765,3.36250770672545,3.34406482519078,3.32548806116878,3.30678541825449,3.28796476837326,3.26891816479142,3.24916944812916,3.22875780528367,3.20772135836091,3.18609718086863,3.16392131458352,3.14122878690512,3.11805362853251,3.0944288913221,3.0703866662047,3.04595810105827,3.02117341844935,2.99606193317097,2.9706520695184,2.94497137825596,2.91904655323929,2.89290344766647,2.86656708994052,2.8400616991326,2.8134107000425,2.78663673785797,;:</isee:data_manager>
	<model_units/>
	<model>
		<variables>
			<stock name="Motivation">
				<doc>
          Initial value = 50. Range strictly 0 to 100.
          Represents student drive and willingness to study.
          The inflow valve uses saturation: (1 - Motivation/100)
          so the gain rate naturally approaches zero as the stock fills.
          This prevents the stock from ever exceeding 100.
        </doc>
				<eqn>50</eqn>
				<inflow>Motivation_Gain</inflow>
				<outflow>Motivation_Loss</outflow>
				<non_negative/>
			</stock>
			<stock name="Knowledge">
				<doc>
          Initial value = 10. Range strictly 0 to 100.
          Accumulated understanding of course material.
          Inflow uses saturation (1 - Knowledge/100) so growth
          slows automatically as knowledge approaches 100.
        </doc>
				<eqn>10</eqn>
				<inflow>Learning_Rate</inflow>
				<outflow>Forgetting_Rate</outflow>
				<non_negative/>
			</stock>
			<stock name="Career Readiness">
				<doc>
          Initial value = 20. Range strictly 0 to 100.
          Combined career aspiration and job prospects.
          Inflow uses saturation (1 - Career_Readiness/100).
        </doc>
				<eqn>20</eqn>
				<inflow>Career_Gain</inflow>
				<outflow>Career_Loss</outflow>
				<non_negative/>
			</stock>
			<flow name="Motivation Gain">
				<doc>
          SATURATION FORMULA — keeps Motivation inside 0-100.

          The term MAX(0, (100-Motivation)/100) is the saturation factor:
            - When Motivation = 0:   factor = 1.0  (full gain rate)
            - When Motivation = 50:  factor = 0.5  (half gain rate)
            - When Motivation = 100: factor = 0.0  (gain stops — stock cannot exceed 100)

          Base components:
            Motivation * 0.10        = R1 reinforcing loop (self-amplifying drive)
            5.0                      = social support floor (prevents total collapse)
            Social_Support * 0.08    = external support contribution
            Career_Readiness * 0.04  = career visibility boosts motivation

          At t=0 (Motivation=50, CR=20, SS=20):
            = (50*0.10 + 5.0 + 20*0.08 + 20*0.04) * (50/100)
            = (5 + 5 + 1.6 + 0.8) * 0.5 = 12.4 * 0.5 = 6.2 /week
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, (Motivation * 0.10 + 5.0 + Social_Support * 0.08 + Career_Readiness * 0.04) * MAX(0, (100 - Motivation) / 100))</eqn>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Motivation Loss">
				<doc>
          Mass-action drain. No saturation needed — outflow naturally
          shrinks as stock shrinks (self-limiting).

          At t=0 (Motivation=50, SP=1.0, BU=0):
            = 50 * (0.03 + 0.003 + 0) = 50 * 0.033 = 1.65 /week

          Net at t=0: 6.2 - 1.65 = +4.55 /week (strong early growth).
        </doc>
				<eqn>Motivation * (0.03 + Stress_Proxy * 0.003 + Burnout * 0.004)</eqn>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Learning Rate">
				<doc>
          SATURATION FORMULA — keeps Knowledge inside 0-100.

          The saturation factor MAX(0,(100-Knowledge)/100):
            - When Knowledge = 10:  factor = 0.90 (near-full rate)
            - When Knowledge = 50:  factor = 0.50 (half rate)
            - When Knowledge = 100: factor = 0.00 (stops at ceiling)

          Coefficient 1.8 replaces original 0.9 to compensate for
          the saturation halving the effective rate at mid-range.

          The expertise term (1 + Knowledge*0.004) adds up to 40%
          bonus at Knowledge=100, rewarding prior learning.

          At t=0 (ST=2.58, SE=0.91, K=10):
            = 2.58 * 0.91 * 1.8 * 1.04 * 0.90 = 3.95 * 0.90 = 3.55 /week
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, Study_Time * Study_Efficiency * 1.8 * (1 + Knowledge * 0.004) * MAX(0, (100 - Knowledge) / 100))</eqn>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Forgetting Rate">
				<doc>
          Mass-action decay — no saturation needed (self-limiting as stock shrinks).
          Study_Efficiency slows forgetting through active recall.
          At t=0 (K=10, SE=0.91): 10 * 0.04 * (1-0.546) = 0.18 /week.
        </doc>
				<eqn>Knowledge * 0.04 * (1 - Study_Efficiency * 0.6)</eqn>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Career Gain">
				<doc>
          SATURATION FORMULA — keeps Career_Readiness inside 0-100.
          Same saturation pattern as the other inflows.

          Drivers: academic knowledge (K*0.05), student drive (M*0.04),
          and engagement hours (ST*0.30 — employers see attendance).

          At t=0 (K=10, M=50, ST=2.58, CR=20):
            = (0.5 + 2.0 + 0.774) * 0.80 = 3.274 * 0.80 = 2.62 /week
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, (Knowledge * 0.05 + Motivation * 0.04 + Study_Time * 0.30) * MAX(0, (100 - Career_Readiness) / 100))</eqn>
			</flow>
			<flow name="Career Loss">
				<doc>
          Mass-action drain. Opportunities expire and ambition erodes under stress.
          At t=0 (CR=20, SP=1.0, BU=0): 20 * (0.015+0.002) = 0.34 /week.
          Net Career at t=0: 2.62 - 0.34 = +2.28 /week.
        </doc>
				<eqn>Career_Readiness * (0.015 + Stress_Proxy * 0.002 + Burnout * 0.003)</eqn>
			</flow>
			<aux name="Discipline">
				<doc>Policy lever. Self-regulation 0-100. BASE=45. IMPROVED=75. At 63+ procrastination=0.</doc>
				<eqn>45</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Sleep Quality">
				<doc>Lifestyle factor 0-100. BASE=38. IMPROVED=78. Affects Study_Efficiency and Burnout.</doc>
				<eqn>38</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Social Support">
				<doc>External support 0-100. BASE=20. IMPROVED=65. Feeds Motivation_Gain directly.</doc>
				<eqn>20</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Exam Pressure">
				<doc>Rises linearly 10→100 over 30 weeks. IMPROVED: use TIME*1.8 instead of TIME*3.</doc>
				<eqn>MIN(100, 10 + TIME * 3)</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Procrastination">
				<doc>Computed from Discipline. At Discipline=45: Procrastination=14. At Discipline=63+: zero.</doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, 50 - Discipline * 0.8)</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Stress Proxy">
				<doc>
          Algebraic stress estimate (replaces stock to stay within 3-stock limit).
          Knowledge and Career_Readiness buffer exam pressure.
          At t=0: 10*0.6 - 10*0.2 - 20*0.15 = 6-2-3 = 1.0
          At W30 (K=69,CR=48,EP=100): 60-13.8-7.2 = 39.0
        </doc>
				<eqn>MIN(100, MAX(0, Exam_Pressure * 0.6 - Knowledge * 0.2 - Career_Readiness * 0.15))</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Burnout">
				<doc>
          Appears when stress exceeds sleep recovery capacity.
          At t=0 (SP=1.0, Sleep=38): MAX(0, 0.4-11.4) = 0.
          Burnout only triggers when SP &gt; Sleep*0.75 = 28.5 (base).
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0, Stress_Proxy * 0.4 - Sleep_Quality * 0.3)</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Study Time">
				<doc>
          Hours/day. Floor=0.5 (minimum study), ceiling=6.
          At t=0 (M=50, Proc=14): 6*(0.5)*(1-0.112) = 3*0.888 = 2.66 hrs/day.
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0.5, 6 * (Motivation / 100) * (1 - Procrastination * 0.008))</eqn>
			</aux>
			<aux name="Study Efficiency">
				<doc>
          Quality multiplier 0.1-1.0. Improved by sleep; degraded by stress and burnout.
          At t=0 (SP=1.0, BU=0, Sleep=38): MAX(0.1, MIN(1.0, 0.8-0.005+0.114)) = 0.91.
        </doc>
				<eqn>MAX(0.1, MIN(1.0, 0.8 - Stress_Proxy * 0.005 - Burnout * 0.007 + Sleep_Quality * 0.003))</eqn>
			</aux>
		</variables>
